+
+Node names with spaces
+----------------------
+A node name (``str(node)``) that is empty or holds whitespace, the
+delimiter, ``#``, ``"`` or ``\\`` is written in double quotes, with
+``\\`` and ``"`` escaped by a backslash (``"New York"``, ``"say \\"hi\\""``).
+Readers take a token that starts with ``"`` as one quoted name, so such
+graphs round-trip. Edge data is written and read as before.
+
+Errors
+------
+The ``parse_*`` and ``read_*`` functions raise
+:exc:`~networkx.LineParseError` (a ``TypeError``) for a line they cannot
+read. It says which line: ``line 3: Failed to convert ...``, and from a
+``read_*`` function with the file name, ``graph.txt:3: Failed to convert
+...``. Its attributes are `message`, `lineno` (from 1, comment and blank
+lines counted), `line` and `filename`.
+
+Sorted output
+-------------
+With ``sort=True`` the ``generate_*`` and ``write_*`` functions write the
+nodes, the neighbours of each node and parallel edges in the order of their
+``str``, an undirected edge from the end that sorts first. Two graphs with
+the same nodes and edges then give the same lines, whatever the order in
+which they were built.
+
+Number format
+-------------
+``float_format`` (a format spec such as ``".3g"``) sets how the
+``generate_*`` and ``write_*`` functions write float values of edge data:
+``{'weight': 0.333}`` instead of ``{'weight': 0.3333333333333333}``, and
+``1 2 0.333`` for ``data=("weight",)``. Keys and other values are written as
+before.
+
+Encodings
+---------
+The ``read_*`` functions skip a UTF-8 byte order mark at the start of the
+file, and with ``encoding=None`` take the encoding from the byte order mark
+(UTF-8, UTF-16 LE or UTF-16 BE; UTF-8 when there is none). The ``write_*``
+functions write a byte order mark first with ``bom=True``.
+
+Line ends
+---------
+The readers take lines that end with ``\\n``, ``\\r\\n`` or ``\\r``; the
+line end is never part of a name or of edge data. The writers end each line
+with `newline` (``"\\n"`` by default, ``"\\r\\n"`` for Windows files).
+
+Parsing
+-------
+The ``parse_*`` functions of the edge list, adjacency list and multiline
+adjacency list are :class:`~networkx.readwrite._lineparser.LineParser`
+methods: ``parse_edgelist(lines, comments, delimiter, ...)`` is
+``LineParser(comments, delimiter, nodetype).parse_edgelist(lines, ...)``.
+
+Writing
+-------
+The ``generate_*`` functions of the edge list, adjacency list and multiline
+adjacency list are :class:`~networkx.readwrite._linewriter.LineWriter`
+methods: ``generate_adjlist(G, delimiter, ...)`` is
+``LineWriter(delimiter, ...).adjlist(G)``.
+
+Files
+-----
+The ``read_*`` and ``write_*`` functions read and write the lines of a file
+through :class:`~networkx.readwrite._textfile.TextFile`:
+``TextFile(encoding).read_lines(file)`` and
+``TextFile(encoding, ...).write_lines(file, lines)``.
